#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:7
msgid ""
"Mattermost provides OpenID Connect support for :doc:`GitLab "
"</administration-guide/onboard/sso-gitlab>`, :doc:`Google Apps "
"</administration-guide/onboard/sso-google>`, and :doc:`Entra ID "
"</administration-guide/onboard/sso-entraid>`. With OpenID Connect, users "
"can also use their login to Keycloak, Atlassian Crowd, Apple, Microsoft, "
"Salesforce, Auth0, Ory.sh, Facebook, Okta, OneLogin, and Azure AD, as "
"well as others, as a Single Sign-on (SSO) service for team creation, "
"account creation, and user login."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:9
msgid "Follow these steps to configure a service provider using OpenID Connect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:12
msgid "Step 1: Create an OpenID Connect Application"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:14
msgid ""
"Follow service provider documentation for creating an OpenID Connect "
"application. Most OpenID Connect service providers require authorization "
"of all redirect URIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:15
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"In the appropriate field, enter ``{your-mattermost-"
"url}/signup/openid/complete`` For example: "
"``http://domain.com/signup/openid/complete``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:16
msgid ""
"Copy and paste values for the **Discovery Endpoint**, **Client ID**, and "
"**Client Secret** values to a temporary location. You will enter these "
"values when you configure Mattermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:19
msgid "Step 2: Configure Mattermost for an OpenID Connect SSO"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:21
msgid ""
"Log in to Mattermost, then go to **System Console > Authentication > "
"OpenID Connect**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:22
msgid "Select **OpenID Connect (Other)** as the service provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:23
msgid "Enter the **Discovery Endpoint**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:24
msgid "Enter the **Client ID**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:25
msgid "Enter the **Client Secret**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:26
msgid ""
"Specify a **Button Name** and **Button Color** for the OpenID Connect "
"option on the Mattermost login page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:27
msgid "Select **Save**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:28
msgid "Restart your Mattermost server to see the changes take effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:31
msgid ""
"When Mattermost is configured to use OpenID Connect for user "
"authentication, the following user attribute changes can't be made "
"through the Mattermost API: first name, last name, or username. OpenID "
"Connect must be the authoritative source for these user attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:32
msgid ""
"Admins can configure Mattermost to use the ``preferred_username`` claim "
"from the OpenID token as the Mattermost username. Enable the **Use "
"preferred username** option in the provider's settings under **System "
"Console > Authentication > OpenID Connect**. See the :ref:`authentication"
" configuration settings <administration-guide/configure/authentication-"
"configuration-settings:openid connect>` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:33
msgid ""
"The **Discovery Endpoint** setting can be used to determine the "
"connectivity and availability of arbitrary hosts. System admins concerned"
" about this can use custom admin roles to limit access to modifying these"
" settings. See the :ref:`delegated granular administration "
"<administration-guide/onboard/delegated-granular-administration:edit "
"privileges of admin roles (advanced)>` documentation for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:36
msgid "Frequently Asked Questions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:39
msgid "How can I use LDAP attributes or Groups with OpenID?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/sso-openidconnect.rst:41
msgid ""
"At this time, LDAP data isn't compatible with OpenID. If you currently "
"rely on LDAP to manage your users' teams, channels, groups, or "
"attributes, you won't be able to do this automatically with users who "
"have logged in with OpenID. If you need LDAP synced to each user, we "
"suggest using SAML or LDAP as the login provider. Some OpenID providers "
"can use SAML instead, like Keycloak."
msgstr ""

